/*****************************************************************************
    dotNameT -- THE DOT'S RIGHT OPERAND IS A NAME, NEVER A VALUE.

    Landed 2026-09-10. Before it, `A.B` on a member name read 0: the right
    operand arrived RESOLVED, and a resolved node WITH DATA returns its DATA
    from .text (bear-trap 26), so the lookup key was the member's whole
    contents instead of its name.

    ⚠ dnKid CARRIES DATA ON PURPOSE, and that is the whole discriminator. A
    data-less member returns its own TAG from .text anyway (bear-trap 26), so a
    fixture built on one passes with the fix REMOVED -- measured, on the first
    cut of this file, when its H7 control stayed green. Only a member with data
    can tell the two roads apart.

    Four rows and they are not separable. DN-1 is the capability. DN-2 is the
    MISS, which has to stay empty or the fix would be minting nodes for names
    that do not exist. DN-3 is the ACCESSOR EXEMPTION -- a groupFields entry is
    selected by REGISTRY MEMBERSHIP and re-minting it would strip that, taking
    the whole accessor family off its road, so it must NOT be re-minted and it
    must still read. DN-0 is the anti-vacuity control.

    Header is prose on purpose -- bear-trap 27.
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(utilities);
search reset stack Grokking UnitTests Utilities list;

register(DotName);
define
    dnKid="a member WITH DATA -- this is the discriminator"; dnOther;
    dnBag   dnKid dnOther;
    dnRes;
    dnRun code={
        cerr "DN-0 control  dnBag.listLengtH        = " dnBag.listLengtH " (want 2 -- the bag really has two)":;
        dnRes := dnBag.dnKid;
        cerr "DN-1 member   dnBag.dnKid       taG   = " *dnRes.taG " (want dnKid)":;
        dnRes := dnBag.zzNoSuchMember;
        cerr "DN-2 miss     dnBag.zzNoSuchMember    = " *dnRes.taG " (want 0 -- a miss mints nothing)":;
        cerr "DN-3 accessor dnBag.noPrinT  BEFORE   = " dnBag.noPrinT " (want 0)":;
        dnBag :. noPrinT;
        cerr "DN-4 accessor dnBag.noPrinT  AFTER    = " dnBag.noPrinT " (want 1 -- DN-3's non-zero sibling; a dead accessor reads 0 both times)":;
        };
    ;
dnRun();
print "DOTNAME SENTINEL -- reached the foot":;
stop();
